    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing out as the unequivocal anchor of the lineup. With a massive 79.66 efficiency score, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a premier matchup against Quintana, whose 5.24 xERA is the softest on the board today. The 19% SP skill boost and his prime #2 spot in the order make him the primary engine for both run production and our scarcity-driven focus on stolen bases. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier are **Josh Naylor** (72.02) and **James Wood** (69.92). **James Wood** is particularly well-positioned; his xwOBA of .379 combined with the leadoff slot against the vulnerable Perez makes him a high-floor play, while **Josh Naylor** leverages a 10% SP skill advantage against Lugo to solidify the middle of our order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jose Caballero**. While he was our strongest depth option (47.06), he was ultimately edged out by **Cole Young** and **Dalton Rushing** due to a combination of unfavorable weather (wind in) and a lower-leverage #7 lineup spot. **Zach McKinstry** remains a sneaky, high-upside start today; despite a lower base projection, his 16% park factor boost and 19% matchup edge against Young elevate him to a 65.79 score, proving that his leadoff deployment is worth the gamble. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains locked in at UTIL, buoyed by a significant 14% platoon advantage against Woo.\n\nWe are keeping a watchful eye on **Brice Turang** (49.06) and **Cole Young** (47.80), both of whom are facing elite-level control in Yamamoto and Lugo, respectively. The scarcity of stolen bases mandates we keep **Brice Turang** active despite the SP difficulty, as his ability to disrupt the battery remains vital to our strategy. With **Mickey Moniak** still sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested; we continue to monitor the status of **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte** to ensure we maintain maximum efficiency across our bench slots. Monitor weather reports closely, as any wind shifts could further suppress the ceilings of our lower-scored starters.",
